nceError</code>. However, if <code>var bar</code> were used, it would be <c=
ode>TypeError</code>. With <code>const</code>, it's actually <code>Referenc=
eError: Cannot access 'bar' before initialization</code>.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Corrected Answer: B) =E2=80=94 Note:</strong> With =
<code>const</code>, accessing <code>bar</code> before its declaration throw=
s <code>ReferenceError: Cannot access 'bar' before initialization</code> du=
e to the Temporal Dead Zone. With <code>var</code>, it would be <code>TypeE=
rror: bar is not a function</code>.</p>
</details>
