<p dir=3D"auto">What is the purpose of this pattern?</p>
<ul dir=3D"auto">
<li>A) Retry failed fetches automatically</li>
<li>B) Add a maximum wait time for the fetch =E2=80=94 if it takes longer t=
han <code>ms</code>, reject with Timeout</li>
<li>C) Run the fetch and timeout in parallel and use whichever resolves fir=
st</li>
<li>D) Both B and C =E2=80=94 they describe the same behavior</li>
</ul>
<details>
<summary><strong>Answer &amp; Explanation</strong></summary>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Answer: D) Both B and C =E2=80=94 they describe the=
 same behavior</strong></p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Explanation:</strong> <code>Promise.race</code> res=
olves/rejects with the first settled promise. If <code>fetch</code> complet=
es before <code>ms</code> milliseconds, it wins. If the timeout resolves fi=
rst, it rejects with <code>"Timeout"</code>. The <code>catch</code> returns=
 a descriptive string. This pattern effectively enforces a max wait time =
=E2=80=94 implementing both a timeout and parallel execution.</p>
</details>
