<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Answer: C) This correctly attaches a bearer token a=
nd implements a 5-second timeout using <code>AbortController</code></strong=
></p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Explanation:</strong> <code>AbortController</code> =
and its <code>signal</code> allow cancelling a <code>fetch</code> request. =
When <code>abort()</code> is called, the Promise rejects with an <code>Abor=
tError</code>. This pattern combines: auth header attachment, a 5-second ti=
meout using <code>setTimeout</code>, and cleanup with <code>clearTimeout</c=
ode> on success. <code>AbortController</code> actually cancels the underlyi=
ng network request, not just the Promise.</p>
</details>
