<details>
<summary><strong>Answer &amp; Explanation</strong></summary>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Answer: B) <code>DocumentFragment</code> batches al=
l nodes and triggers a single reflow/repaint on insertion</strong></p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Explanation:</strong> Each <code>appendChild</code>=
 to a live DOM element can trigger reflow/repaint. <code>DocumentFragment</=
code> is an off-screen container =E2=80=94 nodes added to it don't trigger =
reflows. When the fragment is appended to the DOM, all its children are ins=
erted in one operation =E2=80=94 a single reflow/repaint. For 1000 items, t=
his is a significant performance gain.</p>
</details>
