<ul dir=3D"auto">
<li>A) Virtual DOM is faster than real DOM for every operation</li>
<li>B) Virtual DOM minimizes expensive real DOM operations by computing the=
 minimal diff (reconciliation) needed and applying only those changes in ba=
tch</li>
<li>C) Virtual DOM stores data in memory, avoiding network requests</li>
<li>D) Virtual DOM is only useful for server-side rendering</li>
</ul>
<details>
<summary><strong>Answer &amp; Explanation</strong></summary>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Answer: B) Virtual DOM minimizes expensive real DOM=
 operations by computing the minimal diff (reconciliation) needed and apply=
ing only those changes in batch</strong></p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Explanation:</strong> Direct DOM manipulation is ex=
pensive (triggers reflow/repaint). Virtual DOM frameworks (React, Vue) main=
tain an in-memory representation of the DOM. When state changes, a new virt=
ual DOM is computed and <strong>diffed</strong> against the previous one. O=
nly the minimal set of actual DOM changes is applied. For frequent updates,=
 this batching approach can significantly reduce layout thrashing.</p>
</details>
