<details>
<summary><strong>Answer &amp; Explanation</strong></summary>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Answer: B) Dividing the bundle into smaller chunks =
that are loaded on demand, reducing initial load time</strong></p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Explanation:</strong> Code splitting (via <code>imp=
ort()</code>, webpack, Rollup) divides the app into chunks. Only the initia=
l chunk loads at startup; other chunks load when needed (route change, user=
 interaction). This reduces Time to First Byte (TTFB) and Time to Interacti=
ve (TTI). Combined with lazy loading and route-based splitting, it dramatic=
ally improves perceived performance for large SPAs.</p>
</details>
