<details>
<summary><strong>Answer &amp; Explanation</strong></summary>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Answer: B) The Mediator centralizes inter-component=
 communication =E2=80=94 components don't talk to each other directly, redu=
cing coupling</strong></p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Explanation:</strong> The Mediator acts as a hub. C=
omponents (colleagues) communicate through the mediator, not directly with =
each other. This reduces dependencies from O(n=C3=82=C2=B2) (all-to-all) to=
 O(n) (all-to-mediator). Examples: air traffic control (planes =C3=A2=E2=80=
=A0=E2=80=9D tower =C3=A2=E2=80=A0=E2=80=9D planes), chat rooms (users =C3=
=A2=E2=80=A0=E2=80=9D server =C3=A2=E2=80=A0=E2=80=9D users), React's lifti=
ng state up, Redux store. Contrast with Observer: Mediator has logic; Pub-S=
ub is passive.</p>
</details>
