<li>A) Clickjacking is when a script steals click events; prevented by <cod=
e>stopPropagation()</code></li>
<li>B) Clickjacking overlays a transparent iframe over a legitimate page to=
 trick users into clicking on the hidden target; prevented by <code>X-Frame=
-Options</code> or CSP <code>frame-ancestors</code></li>
<li>C) Clickjacking is a type of XSS attack; prevented by input sanitizatio=
n</li>
<li>D) Clickjacking only affects mobile browsers</li>
</ul>
<details>
<summary><strong>Answer &amp; Explanation</strong></summary>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Answer: B) Clickjacking overlays a transparent ifra=
me over a legitimate page to trick users into clicking on the hidden target=
; prevented by <code>X-Frame-Options</code> or CSP <code>frame-ancestors</c=
ode></strong></p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Explanation:</strong> Clickjacking embeds your site=
 in a transparent <code>&lt;iframe&gt;</code> over a fake UI. A user clicks=
 the fake button but actually clicks a button on your site (e.g., "Transfer=
 Money"). Prevention: <code>X-Frame-Options: DENY</code> (don't embed in if=
rames at all) or CSP <code>frame-ancestors 'none'</code> (modern equivalent=
). React apps should include these headers at the server level.</p>
</details>
