<details>
<summary><strong>Answer &amp; Explanation</strong></summary>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Answer: B) <code>IntersectionObserver</code> effici=
ently detects when elements enter/exit the viewport without scroll event li=
steners, enabling lazy loading</strong></p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Explanation:</strong> <code>IntersectionObserver</c=
ode> uses the browser's internal intersection detection =E2=80=94 no scroll=
 event listeners, no <code>getBoundingClientRect</code> polling. The browse=
r batches notifications, firing callbacks asynchronously. This pattern for =
lazy loading images is highly performant: images load only when they scroll=
 near the viewport, reducing initial load size dramatically.</p>
</details>
