<summary><strong>Answer &amp; Explanation</strong></summary>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Answer: B) Returns cached response if available; fa=
lls back to network if not cached</strong></p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Explanation:</strong> Cache-First prioritizes the c=
ache for speed, making the app work offline or in low-network conditions. I=
f the resource is not cached, it fetches from the network. Contrast with Ne=
twork-First (tries network, falls back to cache) for frequently updated con=
tent.</p>
</details>
