<details>
<summary><strong>Answer &amp; Explanation</strong></summary>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Answer: B) The Push API allows servers to send mess=
ages to Service Workers even when the app is closed</strong></p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Explanation:</strong> Push works even when the brow=
ser is closed: the push service (browser vendor's) receives the server's me=
ssage and wakes the Service Worker. <code>event.waitUntil</code> keeps the =
SW alive while showing the notification. The user must grant notification p=
ermission. The server sends pushes via the Web Push Protocol using VAPID ke=
ys. This enables PWAs to re-engage users like native apps.</p>
</details>
