<ul dir=3D"auto">
<li>A) The recursive <code>connect</code> call will cause a stack overflow<=
/li>
<li>B) This implements exponential backoff reconnection =E2=80=94 retrying =
with increasing delays up to 30s, avoiding server hammering during outages<=
/li>
<li>C) WebSockets reconnect automatically =E2=80=94 this is unnecessary</li=
>
<li>D) <code>setTimeout</code> in <code>onclose</code> causes memory leaks<=
/li>
</ul>
<details>
<summary><strong>Answer &amp; Explanation</strong></summary>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Answer: B) Exponential backoff reconnection =E2=80=
=94 increasing delays up to 30s</strong></p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Explanation:</strong> WebSockets don't auto-reconne=
ct. Exponential backoff: 1s =E2=86=92 2s =E2=86=92 4s =E2=86=92 8s =E2=86=
=92 ... =E2=86=92 30s (capped). This prevents overwhelming a recovering ser=
ver with reconnection storms. The <code>setTimeout</code> callback holds a =
reference to the class instance via closure =E2=80=94 no stack overflow sin=
ce it's not recursive via the call stack, it's via the event loop. In produ=
ction, also reset delay on successful reconnection.</p>
</details>
