<li>B) Exposing internals (models, validators, crypto) creates coupling; co=
nsumers depend on implementation details that change; a clean public API wi=
th use-case-oriented functions hides internals</li>
<li>C) Internal functions should also be exported for testing</li>
<li>D) <code>export type</code> is TypeScript-only and should be avoided fo=
r compatibility</li>
