<details>
<summary><strong>Answer &amp; Explanation</strong></summary>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Answer: B) Exposing internals creates coupling; a c=
lean public API hides implementation details</strong></p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Explanation:</strong> Leaking internals means consu=
mers couple to <code>UserModel</code>, <code>hashPassword</code>, etc. If y=
ou switch from bcrypt to argon2, all consumers break. Clean API: export onl=
y what consumers need (use cases, not mechanisms). For testing internals, u=
se testing-specific exports or test through the public API. Follow the prin=
ciple of least privilege =E2=80=94 expose the minimum needed.</p>
