<details>
<summary><strong>Answer &amp; Explanation</strong></summary>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Answer: B) Return an error map instead of throwing =
=E2=80=94 enables field-level error display and partial validation</strong>=
</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Explanation:</strong> Form validation is not "excep=
tional" =E2=80=94 invalid user input is an expected case, not an error. Thr=
owing exceptions for validation creates awkward try/catch in form handlers.=
 Returning an error map: enables per-field inline errors (red border + mess=
age under each field); supports submit-button enable/disable based on <code=
>isValid</code>; allows progressive validation on blur. Libraries like Yup,=
 Zod, and <code>react-hook-form</code> use this pattern.</p>
</details>
