<summary><strong>Answer &amp; Explanation</strong></summary>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Answer: B) Implement a shared state bus using <code=
>BroadcastChannel</code> API or a shared event bus in the shell, making the=
 shell the single owner of shared state</strong></p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Explanation:</strong> <code>localStorage</code> has=
 no locking mechanism =E2=80=94 concurrent writes from multiple tabs/frames=
 create race conditions. The architectural fix is to designate the shell as=
 the single source of truth for shared state, with micro-frontends communic=
ating via a <code>CustomEvent</code> bus or <code>BroadcastChannel</code> (=
for cross-tab sync). Each micro-frontend dispatches actions; the shell upda=
tes the store and broadcasts changes. <code>IndexedDB</code> transactions p=
revent corruption but don't solve the cross-MFE ownership problem.</p>
</details>
